PACK store 1
RESIDENT Store
-- THE STORE DRIVER (the operator, 2026-11-10): the seat's SQLite store, read by the engine itself -- no Python in the
-- data path. Built-ins, in any getter or setter of any pack:
--   sql(query, args...)  a read (SELECT / WITH; anything else is refused), arguments bound by `?`, rows as dicts;
--                        as the official drivers: no time limit, no row cap, a lock waited for up to 5 s. Thread-safe and
--                        non-blocking: the engine's own read-only connection (WAL: it never waits for the seat's
--                        writer), run off the seat's loop.
--   json(text)           a row's JSON body as a dict (an Error when the text is not JSON); str(x) a value as text.
-- Tables of a store made by cliffvm: `c_field` (k = the eid, cls, updated, body = {props, writers}: the entities) and `c_journal` (the outside writes); `Store:field` shows what is there.
--   A store that came from the 0.7 Python seat has tables of its own (`c_events`, `c_sessions`, `c_messages`, `c_entities`, ... with body = {"o": <order>, "d": {...the document...}}):
--   it is read through a `SqlSource` (packs/sql.c1f), never as this store. json_extract(body, '$.d.<field>') reads one field of such a row.

Store.tables getter: FOR r IN sql("SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = 'table' AND substr(name, 1, 2) = 'c_' ORDER BY name"): ${r}['name']
Store.events getter: max([${r}['n'] for r in sql("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM c_events")]) if this.counted else None
